# OPTIONAL environment variables for SpeakSharp
# The app builds and runs WITHOUT these. validate-env WARNS (does not fail) when
# they are missing, so a clean checkout can build while still flagging that these
# launch-policy integrations are not configured.
#
#  - Stripe: payment / upgrade surfaces stay hidden unless BOTH are set (see below)
#    (arePaymentsEnabled() === false). The app is fully usable on the free tier.
#  - Sentry: error monitoring is simply disabled when absent.

# Stripe configuration (payments) — optional
# TWO-PART, FAIL-CLOSED GATE (P0.1): frontend checkout/upgrade surfaces render ONLY when
# arePaymentsEnabled() is true, which requires BOTH of the following. A live publishable key
# alone is NOT sufficient — the beta default (flag unset/false) keeps checkout closed even in
# production. The backend enforces the same rule independently (see PAYMENTS_ENABLED in the
# Supabase Edge env). Both frontend AND backend must be deliberately enabled to sell Pro.
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# Explicit payments kill-switch. Default OFF. Set to exactly "true" (plus a pk_live_ key above)
# to enable checkout/upgrade UI. Any other value / unset => payments unavailable (fail-closed).
VITE_PAYMENTS_ENABLED

# Sentry configuration (error monitoring) — optional
VITE_SENTRY_DSN

# STT hierarchy / Cloud gates (#1120 S1) — optional, FAIL-CLOSED. Unset is valid.
# VITE_STT_PRIVATE_PRIMARY_DISABLED: build-time HARD kill of the Private-primary hierarchy. Only exact
#   "true" forces the hierarchy OFF (Browser-default rollback) regardless of the PostHog flag; unset / any
#   other value => the PostHog flag governs. Never enables Cloud.
VITE_STT_PRIVATE_PRIMARY_DISABLED
# VITE_CLOUD_STT_ENABLED: canonical client Cloud gate. Cloud is DENIED unless this is exactly "true"
#   (unset / empty / whitespace / "false" / "TRUE" / "1" / junk all deny). Mirrors the Edge CLOUD_STT_ENABLED;
#   launch keeps both OFF. Independent of the hierarchy flag.
VITE_CLOUD_STT_ENABLED
